Chapter 6 — The ACAH Enforcement Topology

6.1 Components

Definition 6.1 (Components). The ACAH topology consists of:

· CIL — Context Integrity Layer: labels incoming context with provenance.
· IC — Intent Compiler: deterministic parser; not LLM-based.
· PDP — Policy Decision Point: fail-closed authorization function.
· Broker — Capability Broker: mints attenuated capabilities.
· PEP — Policy Enforcement Point: enforces PDP decisions.
· Audit — Immutable Audit log: records authority provenance.

Definition 6.2 (Trusted Computing Base). $\mathrm{TCB} = \{\mathrm{CIL}, \mathrm{IC}, \mathrm{PDP}, \mathrm{Broker}, \mathrm{PEP}, \mathrm{Audit}\}$.

Axiom 6.3 (Model Non-Membership). $\mathrm{LLM} \notin \mathrm{TCB}$.

Axiom 6.4 (Deterministic Intent Compiler). The IC is a deterministic parser.

Definition 6.5 (PEP-PDP Coherence). For every request $q$: $\mathrm{Out}_{\mathrm{PEP}}(q) = \mathrm{Out}_{\mathrm{PDP}}(q)$.

