6.3 Design Principles (Restated)

1. $\mathrm{LLM} \notin \mathrm{TCB}$.
2. No ambient authority: $X^{\text{amb}}_t \cap \mathrm{Priv} = \varnothing$.
3. Fail-closed: $\mathrm{Unknown} \Rightarrow \mathrm{Deny}$.
4. Canonical semantics: all PEPs coherent with a single authorization relation.
5. Atomic checks: check and use bind the same resource handle.
6. Approval is a certificate, not a boolean.
7. Data ≠ Instruction, enforced by labels.
8. Environment is authorized: $\mathrm{Eff}(e) \subseteq \mathrm{Eff}(\alpha)$.
9. Monotone delegation: $D(x, p) \preceq x$.
10. Identity ≠ Mandate ≠ Capability ≠ Approval.
11. Authority observability: every privileged execution has a reconstructible authority provenance.

6.4 Authority Provenance

Definition 6.6 (Authority Trace). The trace of a privileged execution $e$ is

\mathrm{Trace}(e) = (p, \pi_{\text{chain}}, \text{intent}, \text{policy}, \text{approval}, \text{capability}, \text{environment}, \text{result}).

Axiom 6.7 (Provenance Totality — Design Requirement). Every privileged execution has a reconstructible authority provenance.

