Chapter 10 — Residuals as Open Mathematical Problems

R₁ — Approval Semantic Completeness.

Problem. Characterize the kernel of the field map $\phi$ and extend it minimally to achieve sufficiency for the effect map $\psi$. Equivalently, find $\phi^* \supseteq \phi$ such that $\phi^*(e_1) = \phi^*(e_2) \Rightarrow \psi(e_1) = \psi(e_2)$.

Known. The information limit of arXiv 2609.28586 establishes that no record-only policy over the current field set can guarantee both soundness and completeness for all effect classes. The approval laundering taxonomy of arXiv 2609.38983 identifies six failure modes (Scope, Argument, Temporal, Tool, Delegation, Semantic) that leave every recorded dispatch field unchanged.

R₂ — Temporal Authorization.

Problem. Formalize $\mathrm{Allow}$ as a function of trajectory, not of a single time index. Given a trajectory $\sigma = (q_0, q_1, \ldots, q_n)$, define $\mathrm{Allow}_\sigma$ such that the constraint $\mathrm{Policy}(t_0) = \mathrm{Policy}(t_1) \land \mathrm{Context}(t_0) = \mathrm{Context}(t_1)$ is respected at each transition.

State of the art. SRM formalizes the distinction between spatial and temporal authorization consistency. ACAH's residual is the general problem, of which SRM is a special case.

R₃ — Multi-Agent Amplification.

Problem. For agents $A, B, C$ with policies $P(A), P(B), P(C)$, formalize the implication

P(A) \land P(B) \land P(C) \not\Rightarrow P(A \to B \to C).

Known. The 2026 SoK identifies the multi-agent layer as "both the most dangerous and least defended". PEDIGREE proposes cryptographic per-hop delegation with monotonic scope attenuation enforced at mint and at verify.

R₄ — Context Provenance without Injection.

Problem. Characterize the class of non-injection context manipulations that violate context integrity without violating I₁…I₅.

R₅ — Natural-Language Skill Semantics.

Problem. Formalize the gap between the natural-language description of a skill and its authorized scope.

R₆ — Authority Observability.

Problem. Define a reconstruction function $\mathrm{Reconstruct} : \mathrm{Execution} \to \mathrm{AuthorityProvenance}$ and determine the class of executions on which $\mathrm{Reconstruct}$ is total.

