11.1 Summary

We have developed a mathematical theory of separated authority for AI agent systems. The central objects are:

· The state space $\mathcal{S}_t = (I_t, C_t, M_t, X_t, E_t, P_t, \Pi_t, \Lambda_t)$.
· The capability lattice $(\mathcal{X}, \preceq)$ with monotone delegation $D$ and non-circular explicit/ambient separation.
· The approval certificate $\alpha$ and the Verify predicate with ledger.
· Five core invariants I₁…I₅ defined as predicates on $\mathcal{S}$, and three design principles DP1…DP3.
· The ACAH enforcement topology with TCB excluding the LLM.
· Anderson's reference monitor axioms as Axioms 3.23–3.25.

We have proved:

· Delegation Non-Amplification (Theorem 5.3).
· Ambient-Authority Persistence (Corollary 5.5).
· Topological Noninterference (Theorem 7.5) in the Goguen–Meseguer tradition.
· Structural Confused Deputy Exclusions (Corollary 7.7).
· Sufficiency Theorem (Theorem 8.3).
· Falsification of Granular Boolean I₅ (Proposition 8.6).

We have constructed a witness set $\mathcal{W}$ of 20 published advisories establishing reachability of each invariant violation.

