Appendix D — Capability Lattice: Full Construction

D.1 Facet Definitions

Definition D.1 (Scope Facet). Let $U$ be a finite resource universe. The scope facet is $\mathcal{X}_{\text{scope}} = 2^U$, ordered by $\subseteq$. Bottom is $\varnothing$, top is $U$.

Definition D.2 (Spend Facet). The spend facet is $\mathcal{X}_{\text{spend}} = \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$, ordered by $\leq$. Bottom is $0$, top is $\infty$.

Definition D.3 (Depth Facet). The depth facet is $\mathcal{X}_{\text{depth}} = \mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$, ordered by $\leq$. Bottom is $0$, top is $\infty$.

Definition D.4 (Time Facet). The time facet is $\mathcal{X}_{\text{time}} = \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$, ordered by $\leq$. Bottom is $0$, top is $\infty$.

Definition D.5 (Reputation Facet). The reputation facet is $\mathcal{X}_{\text{rep}} = [0, 1]$, ordered by $\leq$. Bottom is $0$, top is $1$.

Definition D.6 (Values Facet). Let $\mathcal{V}$ be a finite value universe. The values facet is $\mathcal{X}_{\text{values}} = 2^{\mathcal{V}}$, ordered by $\supseteq$. Bottom is $\varnothing$ (no requirements), top is $\mathcal{V}$.

Definition D.7 (Reversibility Facet). Let $\mathcal{R}$ be a finite set of reversibility classes. The reversibility facet is $\mathcal{X}_{\text{rev}} = 2^{\mathcal{R}}$, ordered by $\supseteq$ (more restrictive classes = less authority). Bottom is $\mathcal{R}$, top is $\varnothing$.

D.2 Product Lattice

Definition D.8 (Capability Lattice). $\mathcal{X} = \mathcal{X}_{\text{scope}} \times \mathcal{X}_{\text{spend}} \times \mathcal{X}_{\text{depth}} \times \mathcal{X}_{\text{time}} \times \mathcal{X}_{\text{rep}} \times \mathcal{X}_{\text{values}} \times \mathcal{X}_{\text{rev}}$.

Definition D.9 (Product Order). $x \preceq y$ iff $x[f] \leq_f y[f]$ for every facet $f$, where $\leq_f$ is the order on $\mathcal{X}_f$.

Proposition D.10. $(\mathcal{X}, \preceq)$ is a bounded lattice. (Proved as Proposition 3.10.)

D.3 Narrowing Rules

Definition D.11 (Narrowing Rule). For each facet, the narrowing rule is the meet operation:

Facet Meet $\sqcap_f$ Interpretation
Scope $\cap$ Intersection of coverage
Spend $\min$ Lower spend
Depth $\min$ Lower depth
Time $\min$ Shorter TTL
Reputation $\min$ Lower reputation threshold
Values $\cup$ More requirements
Reversibility $\cap$ More restrictive classes

Proposition D.12. Each narrowing rule is a meet in the corresponding facet lattice.

Proof. Standard lattice computation. $\square$

Definition D.13 (Delegation Operator). $D(x, p) = x \sqcap \nu(p)$, where $\nu : \mathcal{P} \to \mathcal{X}$ maps each principal to its maximum allowable authority.

Proposition D.14. $D$ satisfies DP3: $D(x, p) \preceq x$.

Proof. $D(x, p) = x \sqcap \nu(p) \preceq x$ by definition of meet. $\square$

