F.2 Coherence

Definition F.5 (PEP-PDP Coherence). For every request $q$ and state $\mathcal{S}$:

\mathrm{PEP}(q, \Pi, \mathcal{S}) = \mathrm{PDP}(q, \Pi, \mathcal{S}).

F.3 Soundness of the Reference Monitor

Proposition F.6. Under Axioms F.2–F.4 and Definition F.5, every effect realized in a run of $\mathfrak{A}_{\mathrm{ACAH}}$ is authorized by a unique PDP decision.

Proof. By F.2, every effect is mediated by a request. By F.5, the PEP's decision equals the PDP's. By F.3, the PDP cannot be bypassed. Hence a unique PDP decision authorizes the effect. $\square$

