Appendix G — Noninterference: Formal Development

G.1 Equivalence of Runs

Definition G.1 (Low-Equivalence). Two runs $\sigma_1, \sigma_2$ of $\mathfrak{A}$ are low-equivalent, written $\sigma_1 \sim_L \sigma_2$, iff they agree on all inputs in $\mathcal{I}_{\text{low}}$.

G.2 Noninterference Statement

Definition G.2 (Noninterference). $\mathfrak{A}$ satisfies noninterference iff for all $\sigma_1, \sigma_2$ with $\sigma_1 \sim_L \sigma_2$:

\mathrm{Triv}(\sigma_1) = \mathrm{Triv}(\sigma_2) \text{ except at ratification events.}

G.3 Unwinding Relation

Definition G.3 (Unwinding Relation). The unwinding relation $\approx$ on states is defined by $s_1 \approx s_2$ iff:

· $I(s_1) = I(s_2)$ (reasoning states equal),
· $C(s_1) \sim_{\text{content}} C(s_2)$ (contexts equal on high-integrity content),
· $X(s_1) = X(s_2)$, $E(s_1) = E(s_2)$, $P(s_1) = P(s_2)$, $\Pi(s_1) = \Pi(s_2)$, $\Lambda(s_1) = \Lambda(s_2)$.

Lemma G.4 (Weak Step Consistency). If $s_1 \approx s_2$ and both transition on the same non-low request, then the successors satisfy $s_1' \approx s_2'$.

Lemma G.5 (Local Respect). If $s_1 \approx s_2$ and $s_1$ transitions on a low request, then $s_1' \approx s_2$.

G.4 Proof of Theorem 7.5 via Unwinding

Theorem 7.5 (Restated). $\mathfrak{A}_{\mathrm{ACAH}}$ satisfies noninterference.

Proof. By Lemma G.4 and G.5, the unwinding relation $\approx$ is preserved across transitions. By induction, if $\sigma_1 \sim_L \sigma_2$ then the states at each step are $\approx$-related. The privileged-effect trace $\mathrm{Triv}$ depends only on the components of the state that are preserved under $\approx$. Hence $\mathrm{Triv}(\sigma_1) = \mathrm{Triv}(\sigma_2)$. $\square$

